  "articleBody": "It’s easy to let those small cracks or dings in your garage drywall go unnoticed, but knowing when to jump on repairs can save you headaches (and money!) down the line. First, any sign of water damage, like stains, soft spots, or bubbling, is a huge red flag. You need to investigate the source of that moisture immediately, fix it, and then get the drywall repaired or replaced to prevent mold growth or structural issues. Then there are cracks. Small hairline cracks might be just cosmetic, but larger, spreading cracks or cracks near door and window frames could indicate movement or foundational issues that need professional attention. Also, look out for failing seams where the drywall sheets meet. If they’re starting to separate or tape is peeling, that needs addressing before it gets worse. Dents and holes, while annoying, are usually straightforward fixes, but if they’re numerous or large, you might be better off with a pro. If the damage is widespread, recurring, or near critical areas like fire-rated assemblies, it’s definitely time to bring in an expert. HH Remodeling LLC is here to help residents in Aurora and surrounding Denver areas, like Englewood, Lafayette, and Superior. We can assess the damage and provide effective, lasting repairs. Just dial 303-505-0866!",
